WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.607
Zann stared in horror as the energy flowed toward a wormhole blinking in the corner.

2
00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:13.754
Through the opening he caught a glimpse of the rough bark of the ancient Wormwood tree.

3
00:00:13.755 --> 00:00:17.658
It was too late—Magica was about to be destroyed!

4
00:00:17.659 --> 00:00:21.723
Suddenly Zann had an idea. He turned to the queen.

5
00:00:21.724 --> 00:00:25.368
"Your Majesty, summon all the wormholes!"

6
00:00:25.369 --> 00:00:30.960
For a second the Roodian queen looked confused. Then her eyes widened.

7
00:00:30.961 --> 00:00:34.620
She raised a hand, and the air buzzed with new energy.

8
00:00:34.621 --> 00:00:40.270
"What are you doing?" Morb snarled, still weakened from the mice's feeding.

9
00:00:40.271 --> 00:00:44.231
Suddenly the room was flooded with thousands of wormholes!

10
00:00:44.232 --> 00:00:49.467
Morb looked stunned. "What—how—" he stammered.

11
00:00:49.468 --> 00:00:54.251
Zann held his breath, hoping he was right about what would happen next.

12
00:00:54.252 --> 00:01:01.458
If he was wrong, he might have just destroyed not only Magica, but also every other world.

13
00:01:01.459 --> 00:01:08.998
He glanced through a nearby wormhole. In a world he didn't recognize, a funny-looking dragon was nibbling on a tree.

14
00:01:08.999 --> 00:01:16.297
Bzzt ! A tiny spurt of energy snaked in and fizzled out against the dragon's scaly

15
00:01:16.298 --> 00:01:21.602
side. Zann spun around and spotted the rough seas of Skellia through another

16
00:01:21.603 --> 00:01:28.202
wormhole. Bzzt ! A gulper leaped up and swallowed a small blob of energy hovering over

17
00:01:28.203 --> 00:01:34.651
the waves. Everywhere he looked, Zann saw bits of energy fizzling out harmlessly in

18
00:01:34.652 --> 00:01:42.216
various worlds. "It worked!" he cried. "The energy got divided into so many different worlds that it became

19
00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:45.558
completely harmless!" "But how did you know that would happen?" Perda

20
00:01:45.559 --> 00:01:53.506
asked. Zann shrugged. "It was what Morb said about how something that's powerful in large amounts is harmless in small

21
00:01:53.507 --> 00:01:59.739
amounts." Morb gnashed his teeth. "I should have killed you when I had the

22
00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:04.550
chance!" "But you didn't." Wyssa stepped forward and snapped her

23
00:02:04.551 --> 00:02:18.357
fingers. Instantly Morb was shackled to her. Then she pointed at the contraption and muttered a few words. Both horns exploded into

24
00:02:18.358 --> 00:02:25.215
shrapnel. Zann and the others ducked, covering their heads until the dust settled. Then Venna stood

25
00:02:25.216 --> 00:02:30.643
up. "Now what are we going to do with Morb?" she asked. "There will have to be a

26
00:02:30.644 --> 00:02:36.356
trial." "Agreed," Zann's mother said. "Nax and I will have plenty of evidence to

27
00:02:36.357 --> 00:02:42.803
present." Zann's father nodded. "I imagine the Red Council will banish him to the Wastelands

28
00:02:42.804 --> 00:02:46.585
forever." Wyssa scowled. "I'll save you all the

29
00:02:46.586 --> 00:02:49.687
trouble." She yanked at Morb, who struggled

30
00:02:49.688 --> 00:02:52.976
weakly. "No!" he cried. "Don't let her take

31
00:02:52.977 --> 00:02:58.307
me!" Zann winced, remembering what Wyssa had said about feeding Morb to a scatter

32
00:02:58.308 --> 00:03:05.330
beast. Then he looked at his parents. Because of Morb, Zann had almost lost them all over

33
00:03:05.331 --> 00:03:09.754
again. Still, did even Morb deserve the fate Wyssa had in mind for

34
00:03:09.755 --> 00:03:17.096
him? "Wait!" Gliss stepped forward. "After you're finished with him"—she glanced at Morb— "will you do something

35
00:03:17.097 --> 00:03:20.424
else?" "What is it, girl?" Wyssa sounded

36
00:03:20.425 --> 00:03:24.026
impatient. "We visited a world called Skellia," Gliss

37
00:03:24.027 --> 00:03:29.950
said. "The waters were rising, and the people were scared. Can you help

38
00:03:29.951 --> 00:03:35.216
them?" Wyssa raised an eyebrow in surprise. "I know Skellia," she

39
00:03:35.217 --> 00:03:42.418
said. Her voice softened. "And yes, if the Skellians are ready to leave, I can

40
00:03:42.419 --> 00:03:47.309
help." Darb stepped forward too. "Also, can you return this mibbit to

41
00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.745
Pax?" "Of course. The Paxians must be worried about

42
00:03:51.746 --> 00:03:56.412
him." Wyssa waited while Darb rubbed the creature's ears before handing it

43
00:03:56.413 --> 00:04:02.931
over. Then she glanced around. "Any other errands you need me to handle for

44
00:04:02.932 --> 00:04:06.761
you?" Her tone was sharp, but Zann caught a twinkle in her

45
00:04:06.762 --> 00:04:12.170
eye. "I think that's it," he said, "but . . ." He hesitated, staring at

46
00:04:12.171 --> 00:04:14.232
Morb. "What are you going to do with

47
00:04:14.233 --> 00:04:19.221
him?" "Only what he deserves." Wyssa gave a jerk on the

48
00:04:19.222 --> 00:04:24.373
shackles. "I'm sure the queen can help direct you all home.

49
00:04:24.374 --> 00:04:27.780
Good-bye." Dragging Morb, Wyssa stepped into the

50
00:04:27.781 --> 00:04:39.271
wormhole. The evil villain cried,

51
00:04:39.272 --> 00:04:44.328
"No!" "Are we there yet?" Zann joked as he and his parents walked toward their

52
00:04:44.329 --> 00:04:47.614
house. Zing was circling overhead, whistling

53
00:04:47.615 --> 00:04:52.676
joyfully. "You tell me, son," his father joked back. "I've never been here

54
00:04:52.677 --> 00:04:57.923
before." After Wyssa had departed with Morb, the Roodian queen sorted through the

55
00:04:57.924 --> 00:05:03.949
wormholes. First she located the one leading into Wormwood, which Venna used to return to First

56
00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:09.572
City. Then, after a long search, the queen found the one leading into Swamp

57
00:05:09.573 --> 00:05:16.522
Bottom. "I can't wait to see what Boz has done with the interior," Zann's father said when they stopped in front of their house.

58
00:05:16.523 --> 00:05:20.933
His wife chuckled. "Don't expect too much," she warned.

59
00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:24.174
"My father was never much of a decorator."

60
00:05:24.175 --> 00:05:28.226
They headed inside. There was no sign of Boz.

61
00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:35.120
"Look!" Zann's mother exclaimed. "Those are the blink images from our trip to the Flower Forest."

62
00:05:35.121 --> 00:05:38.603
She and Zann's father hurried over for a closer look.

63
00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:44.616
Meanwhile Zann heard footsteps. A moment later his grandfather burst into the room.

64
00:05:44.617 --> 00:05:49.399
"Zann!" Boz exclaimed. He rushed over and hugged Zann tightly.

65
00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.389
Then he gently shoved him away and glared.

66
00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.501
"Where in all the worlds have you been?

67
00:05:56.502 --> 00:06:04.506
I've been worried sick! The Directory showed nothing of your whereabouts, and every spell I tried was—"

68
00:06:04.507 --> 00:06:07.236
Zann's mother stepped up behind Boz.

69
00:06:07.237 --> 00:06:11.025
"Hello, Dad," she said. "Did you miss me too?"

70
00:06:11.026 --> 00:06:14.843
Boz's jaw dropped. "Asta?" he whispered.

71
00:06:14.844 --> 00:06:20.651
Then, his nose quivering wildly and his eyes widening, he spun around.

72
00:06:20.652 --> 00:06:25.773
"And Nax too! What—how did you . . .?"

73
00:06:25.774 --> 00:06:30.484
Zann laughed. "We'll tell you all about it!"

74
00:06:30.485 --> 00:06:38.660
That night Zann fell asleep happy. At one point, in the middle of the night, he was awakened by a terrible dream.

75
00:06:38.661 --> 00:06:42.312
Morb had escaped! And Zann's parents were in trouble . . .

76
00:06:42.313 --> 00:06:45.875
But as Zann looked around, he remembered where he was.

77
00:06:45.876 --> 00:06:50.063
He was back in his own bed. His parents and Boz were nearby.

78
00:06:50.064 --> 00:06:53.121
Zing's fiery breath was warming his toes.

79
00:06:53.122 --> 00:07:09.713
For the first time in four years, Zann felt content.

